cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use go-in-lean, its findings or its data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "go-in-lean: bit-precise Lean models and executable evidence for Go correctness bugs"
authors:
  - family-names: Celles
    given-names: Sébastien
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9987-4338"
repository-code: "https://github.com/s-celles/go-in-lean"
url: "https://s-celles.github.io/go-in-lean/"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Bit-precise Lean 4 models of Go, proofs of their documented properties, and
  executable reproducers for the Go compiler and standard library bugs they reveal.
  Disclosure: the author reports issues and contributes fixes to Go, and has
  reported issues to Yaegi, as part of this project; has no funding, employment or
  other interest tied to the systems examined; and works with an AI assistant.
keywords:
  - Go
  - Lean 4
  - compiler testing
  - formal verification
  - translation validation
